        "math_academy_id": "q-120546",
        "problem": "Let $A(1,0,-1)$ and $B(0,1,1).$ Find $|a+2b|,$ where $a$ and $b$ are position vectors of $A$ and $B$, respectively.",
        "worked_solution": "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=i-k, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=j+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates of $a+2b$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2b & =(i-k)+2(j+k) \\\\  & =i+2j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+2b| & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
